# markdown-cost.ratchet -- prose lines in this tree. SHRINKS ONLY.
# Raised only by a hand edit, which is meant to be reviewed. See bin/markdown-cost.sh.
# seeded 2026-08-15 at 19646.
#
# RAISED 2026-08-15 to 20052 (+406), by hand, with the case here.
#
# The branch adds three guards and their three witness suites (#288, #117,
# #282). In a repo whose convention is a documented WHY header per script --
# and whose bin/suite-docs-lint.sh REQUIRES a HERMETICITY note on every suite
# -- six new files cannot be added without prose. Getting to +0 would have
# meant six files carrying no explanation, which is the thing this ratchet is
# meant to protect, not the thing it is meant to prevent.
#
# It was trimmed first, not just raised: the three script headers were cut by
# ~34 lines of restatement before this number was written. What remains is the
# incident each guard exists because of, which is the part that stops the next
# agent re-deriving it.
#
# The ratchet's purpose is to stop UNDIRECTED prose growth -- a tree reaching
# 57% prose one under-threshold commit at a time. It is not a ban on adding
# mechanism. This is the affordance the guard itself names: "make the case in
# review and raise bin/markdown-cost.ratchet by hand."
#
# The first value (19533) was taken before #298, #302, #307, #308 and #310
# landed, so it never described the tree it guarded -- main was already 102
# over it on the day it was written. This is a measurement of main plus the 40
# lines this guard itself costs, trimmed twice to get there. Every later PR is
# judged against a number that is true.
20052
